\newlabel{tab:cost_main}{{6}{8}{Cost-aware head-to-head, $n=200$ per (dataset, condition). Latency is end-to-end per query. Indexing time is the offline cost of building the dataset's retrieval structure. Faithfulness CIs are bootstrap $95\%$ intervals; hallucination CIs are Wilson $95\%$ intervals. RAPTOR-$2$L's indexing cost is $17$--$22\times $ the dense baseline's}{table.caption.26}{}}
